{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Gerrit 2244 patchset 2 — addressed the LLM-Review -1.\n\nBlocking finding (no test drove the actual re-clone/skip paths) fixed by extracting the entrypoint out of the `RUN { echo ...; }` heredoc into a real file, `infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh`, installed onto PATH via `RUN install -m 0755` exactly as Dockerfile.reviewbot installs reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh. Behaviour preserved (same env, same `provision_store &`, same `exec \"$@\"`, same log lines); a `--provision-only` mode was added so the provisioning step can be run synchronously by tests and by an operator debugging a volume.\n\nNew suite tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py executes `provision_store` against a temp dir with a stubbed `git` on PATH: poisoned store (`.git` present, HEAD unresolvable) is cleared + re-cloned; working-tree files with no `.git` at all (the shape seen in production) are cleared + re-cloned; a healthy store is neither cleared nor re-cloned; clone failure and ensure failure both surface in the exit status instead of being swallowed; the rm guard refuses unsafe REBAR_TRACKER_DIR values; a peer-held lock blocks the re-clone; an abandoned lock is broken. Every absence assertion is paired with a liveness anchor (ensure-stub invocation + the terminal `provisioning finished` line).\n\nAdvisories also addressed: `body.index(...)` replaced with a message-bearing `_require()` helper; the `rm -rf` is guarded (non-empty, absolute, not `/`) and additionally clears from inside the directory with relative globs so a bypassed guard is a no-op rather than `rm -rf /*`; the rm+clone is serialized across containers with an atomic mkdir lock, double-checked after acquisition, with a timestamped stale-break so a container dying mid-clone cannot wedge the store the way the original bug did.\n\nAll 9 behaviour mutations verified RED then restored GREEN. 57 tests pass across the three affected suites; make lint, make typecheck, and the complexity ratchet all pass; shellcheck clean on the new script (one intentional SC2016 suppression on the credential-helper body).\n\nNot closing — awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787766501049912624,"uuid":"b446856f-c7da-43b3-be05-07112f38de7f"}